Overview

This document outlines the complete technology stack used for the development and deployment of the educational video management system. The stack is selected for speed, scalability, ease of integration with AI tooling (e.g., Cursor), and support for modern web development practices.

Frontend

Framework: Next.js (React-based)

Styling: Tailwind CSS + SCSS Modules

Component Library: shadcn/ui (Headless UI + Radix)

State Management: React Context API (or optional Zustand in future)

Markdown Editor: TipTap (Notion-style WYSIWYG for documents)

Video Embed: YouTube iframe API

Form Handling: React Hook Form + Zod

Routing: Next.js App Router (app directory)

Auth Handling: Supabase Auth hooks (client-side session)

Backend

Platform: Next.js API Routes (Edge-capable, serverless)

Database: Supabase (PostgreSQL)

Authentication: Supabase Auth (JWT-based)

Access Control: Supabase Row Level Security (RLS)

API Protocol: REST (modular route handlers per feature)

Validation: Zod (shared client/server schemas)

Email/OTP: Supabase Magic Link & Email login

DevOps & Hosting

Frontend + API Hosting: Vercel

Database & Auth: Supabase (managed)

Environment Management: .env.local + Supabase dashboard

Tooling

IDE: VS Code + Cursor AI plugin

Documentation: Markdown (.mdc) docs, generated via CodeGuide

Design System: Figma (optional)

Package Manager: pnpm

APIs & External Services

YouTube Data API: Video title, duration, thumbnail fetch

GitHub: Version control and CI triggers (via Vercel) 